From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] watchdog: dw_wdt: Stop the counter at power-off

The DesignWare watchdog cannot be stopped once started. Where power-off
cuts the power that does not matter, but some firmware sleeps in its
place, keeping the SoC powered for a wake source to start it again:
Rockchip's RK3528 boxes power off so. There the running counter resets
the board a timeout after power-off, an RK3528 box answering again
about 80 s after it was turned off.

At power-off prepare, before such a firmware's handler, gate the
counter's clock as suspend does. The bus clock stays on: the watchdog
core may still ping a running watchdog until the CPUs stop, and a
register access without it can fault. A watchdog with no bus clock of
its own is left as it was.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/watchdog/dw_wdt.c | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/watchdog/dw_wdt.c b/drivers/watchdog/dw_wdt.c
--- a/drivers/watchdog/dw_wdt.c
+++ b/drivers/watchdog/dw_wdt.c
@@ -26,6 +26,7 @@
 #include <linux/of.h>
 #include <linux/platform_device.h>
 #include <linux/pm.h>
+#include <linux/reboot.h>
 #include <linux/reset.h>
 #include <linux/watchdog.h>
 
@@ -552,6 +553,20 @@
 
 #endif /* !CONFIG_DEBUG_FS */
 
+/*
+ * A power-off that leaves the SoC powered, a firmware's sleep in its place,
+ * would have the counter reset the board a timeout later. Stop the counter
+ * as suspend does, keeping the bus clock for a ping still on its way.
+ */
+static int dw_wdt_power_off_prepare(struct sys_off_data *data)
+{
+	struct dw_wdt *dw_wdt = data->cb_data;
+
+	clk_disable_unprepare(dw_wdt->clk);
+
+	return NOTIFY_DONE;
+}
+
 static int dw_wdt_drv_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 {
 	struct device *dev = &pdev->dev;
@@ -673,6 +688,15 @@
 
 	watchdog_set_restart_priority(wdd, 128);
 
+	/* without its own bus clock, the counter's stops register access too */
+	if (dw_wdt->pclk) {
+		ret = devm_register_sys_off_handler(dev, SYS_OFF_MODE_POWER_OFF_PREPARE,
+						    SYS_OFF_PRIO_HIGH,
+						    dw_wdt_power_off_prepare, dw_wdt);
+		if (ret)
+			goto out_assert_rst;
+	}
+
 	ret = watchdog_register_device(wdd);
 	if (ret)
 		goto out_assert_rst;
